{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/720968-kindred-population-numbers","id":720968,"title":"Kindred Population Numbers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T16:38:15-07:00","id":720968,"title":"Kindred Population Numbers?","content":"So, I was looking over setting information in the book, and kindred populations seem... utterly mind bogglingly small. like, Tokyo apparently only has about three hundred vampires... and this is noted as especially high... in an overall city area with over 45 million people. So, I guess I should ask, what human/vampire number ratio do you think is appropriate for a sustainable vampire population without blowing things wide open?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T16:42:56-07:00","id":721001,"title":"","content":"I go about one vampire per one hundred thousand people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:03:40-07:00","id":721146,"title":"","content":"I go one per 50,000-100,000 people. Since the city I'm working on is Portland, OR, that's like 22-44 kindred, approximately. Counting the greater metropolitan area beyond Portland itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T17:30:40-07:00","id":721222,"title":"","content":"Whatever the story requires.<br /> <br /> We've had other threads on the subject, in case the posters don't reappear here you might want to check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population\">here</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/12901-requiem-games-with-low-kindred-populations\">here</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/493772-how-do-you-fit-so-many-vampires-groups-in-smaller-cities-what-ratio-do-you-follow\">this one</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/118740-supernatural-populations\">that one</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/170697-populations\">another one here</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/543689-supernatural-population-sizes\">this one</a>.<br /> <br /> If it matters, the first edition suggested an average ratio of 1 vampire for every 50,000 people in large cities, and 1 vampire for every 100,000 being 'not unusual,' elsewhere, with a caveat that notoriously populous cities such as New York and, perhaps, Tokyo might have even more. However, since Embracing in second edition requires more of an investment, it's possible that vampires aren't as interested in making vast numbers of other Kindred around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T19:04:42-07:00","id":721414,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to keep building NPCs until they stop coming to me or making sense in the setting. I'm not too concerned about the &quot;realism&quot; of it, and I figure my players aren't likely to encounter every vampire in the city regardless, so just expanding outward provides more options without straining credibility.<br /> <br /> That said, I expect my kindred population to average around 100 for a city of about a half million (though I think that half mill number doesn't take into account much of the surrounding area which constitutes a significant part of my setting). I suppose 1 per 5,000 is rather high, but whatever. We're a city with a lot of tourists and business travelers, so that seems like a major factor in supporting a large population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T23:44:06-07:00","id":722076,"title":"","content":"I typically assume 1 : 50,000 with variance depending on mortal security and what the political situation of the vampires are. A city on &quot;wartime footing&quot; with covenants fighting it out might be as high as 1 : 10,000 as hapless mortals are roped in as disposable cannon-fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T23:51:21-07:00","id":722088,"title":"","content":"I typically assume 25-50 vampires per larger city (500.000 upwards) and 20-25 in smaller cities. Simply because that's the numbers you require to adequately populate five clans and five covenants. I usually do write-ups for around 25-30 vampires. That's enough for the player characters in a chronicle to engage with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T04:09:29-07:00","id":722547,"title":"","content":"Tokyo is interesting because the author said he actually originally wrote it as 1000 kindred.<br /> <br /> I tend to think that there isn't really a corelation between mortal population and kindred population. What matters is the limited social space of kindred society. A city generally only has one hierarchy (plus a few covenants ones). That means there's a limited amount of places for a vampire. Ultimately the only place that can really expand a lot is the very bottom and that creates it's own huge problems leading to a general pressure to limit the population which afterall is a key part of the Prince's role.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you have to follow that logic, but it's a reasonable possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T04:38:26-07:00","id":722567,"title":"","content":"I like using population as a guideline, but I do agree that it's the limited social space that matters most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T05:14:48-07:00","id":722635,"title":"","content":"The Kindred population is exactly as big as it needs to be in order to tell the story you want. Everyone has their own way of doing it. I've seen 13 vampires for a city the size of San Diego in one game, and I've seen a nearly 10 thousand vampires for another game. I had a game set on a yacht once with two vampires, a mage, and three changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:38:25-07:00","id":725332,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is the dynamics of vampire politics. A single strong force ruling over all local vampires can mean larger numbers than normal. A fractious society at war with itself could lead to nothing more than a handful of coteries. A caveat to the old ratio is that it was for vampires awake. I think that gets lost. There could be many more vampires in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T13:03:34-07:00","id":729708,"title":"","content":"It probably depends on the nature of the city, as well. Cities with a reputation for danger or with inadequate or especially corrupt police protection might be able to support more vampires, as might cities in parts of the world where things like smartphones are less common. I tend to imagine that particularly dense populations of kindred might exist in the massive slums found in cities like Mumbai and Nairobi. Such places might also have a disproportionate number of very low humanity vampires, though, due to the nightmarish conditions in which they surround themselves.<br /> <br /> It's also been suggested that certain cities seem to attract vampires for whatever reason, usually ones with a popular reputation as centers of nightlife and sinful behavior in general. New Orleans is one of these, and New York is mentioned as well, I think, but I imagine that places like Las Vegas and Los Angeles would qualify as well. Heck, a whole coterie of vampires could probably spend their entire requiem in one of Vegas' massive casino-hotels, without ever having to see the sky if they didn't want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 10-26-2015, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T20:29:02-07:00","id":736664,"title":"","content":"A lot of vampires get killed because they don't really adapt to the All-Night Society. Some get killed even if they adapt, through the machinations of their fellow Kindred, or even through sheer dumb luck. This helps to keep their numbers down. This is without taking into account all the antagonists available: Strixes, Hunters, other splats, even mortal wars. Imagine ISIS or Al Qaeda setting up shop in your town. At the same time.<br /> <br /> Yeah, lots of ways to limit vampire population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5187-aron-times","name":"Aron Times","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5187_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}